    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working with a client who's been stuck at the same weight on their back squat for like 4 weeks now. they're hitting everything else fine but the squat just isn't moving. how do deload weeks or changing up the volume help get past a plateau like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A deload week allows the central nervous system and muscles to recover from accumulated fatigue, which is often the true barrier to progress. Reducing volume and intensity for 5-7 days can refresh your client without losing strength gains. Alternatively, changing things up, such as switching to paused squats or varying the rep scheme, can overload the muscle in a new way, breaking through the current adaptation plateau.",
      "source": "target",
